# Course materials are committed, by Sanjan's decision of 2026-09-09. See the
# permission section of corpus/raw/MANIFEST.md for what was and was not granted.
# corpus/processed/ is regenerable from corpus/raw/ with `ym07 ingest`; it is
# committed so a second machine needs no re-ingest, and may be dropped if it
# starts to drift from the raw material.

# Runs, generated training data and trained adapters are all committed too, by
# Sanjan's decision of 2026-09-12: the material they restate is already
# published. Grounded C2 runs and the generated pairs quote the course notes at
# length, and the adapters are trained on them, which is why they were held back
# until now.
#
# Dry runs produce fake answers and must never be mistaken for evidence. They
# are not distinguishable from real runs by directory name - only manifest.json
# says dry_run - so `git add -A` will happily commit one. Delete dry-run
# directories rather than relying on a rule that cannot see inside them:
#   grep -l '"dry_run": true' runs/*/manifest.json

# Optimizer state is the one exception. Three files of 155-309 MB that do
# nothing but let an interrupted training run resume, and weights this large go
# to Git LFS, whose free tier holds 1 GB in all. The adapter weights themselves
# are committed.
optimizer.pt
grading/review/
grades/model-assisted.jsonl

# LaTeX rebuilds all of these from the .tex files on every run, and they change
# on every run, so committing them would bury the real edits in noise.
# Report/Thesis.pdf is deliberately not listed: the built report is worth keeping
# in the history, and it is the thing that actually gets handed in.
Report/**/*.aux
Report/*.bbl
Report/*.blg
Report/*.toc
Report/*.lof
Report/*.lot
Report/*.lis
Report/*.out
Report/*.log
Report/*.synctex.gz
